Apache-2.0. DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code.

data/lines120.json (Gram and F2^9 labels of the 120 E8 lines, the first 104 being the
P104 ports) is our derived data: the port Gram and labels read from the charts of the
#7334 word family (Clear1nsight), closed under reflections, with the 16 virtual labels
solved over F2. Its 104-port block is checked against the repository file
research/complex-frame-pair-decoders/inputs/pr717/P104_HIT_flip_3a.txt (PR968 decoder,
pinned in SOURCES.json) through data/iso968.json, the same bytes vendored by #7557;
credit the PR968 authors.

data/fiverow-*.txt and data/fiverow-coarse.txt are outputs of our own lane code
(lane/prep.py, lane/prop2.cpp, lane/runcoarse.sh), shipped as provenance; CI does not run
the lane code.

The decoder row pairs (z', z) follow the FANOUT56 factorisation used across our P104
packages. The owned deletion bound and the contract classes are from #7555. Credit ToikY
and the other contributors of the P104 price and replay lineage for the conventions.

All checkers in this package are our own code; no code is imported from the repository or
any other package.
